# Environment variables read by kas-container and the ci/ helper scripts.
# Nothing loads this file: export the variables you need in your shell before
# running the commands. All are optional; each entry gives its type, the
# behaviour when unset, and a safe example. The kas variables are defined by
# kas: https://kas.readthedocs.io/en/latest/command-line/environment-variables.html

# Path to the kas-container script (path). Unset: ci/kas-container-shell-helper.sh
# uses the kas-container found on PATH.
# KAS_CONTAINER=$HOME/bin/kas-container

# Container engine that kas-container uses (docker or podman). Unset: Docker when
# it is installed, otherwise Podman.
# KAS_CONTAINER_ENGINE=podman

# kas work directory for build output and layer checkouts, kept outside the
# repository (path). Unset: kas uses the current directory;
# ci/kas-shell-helper.sh creates a temporary directory.
# KAS_WORK_DIR=$HOME/yocto/kas-work

# Shared download and shared-state cache directories (paths). kas-container passes
# them into the container and ci/oe-selftest.sh writes them to local.conf. Unset:
# each build directory keeps its own downloads/ and sstate-cache/.
# DL_DIR=$HOME/yocto/cache/downloads
# SSTATE_DIR=$HOME/yocto/cache/sstate-cache

# Colon-separated kas files for ci/kas-container-shell-helper.sh (string). Unset:
# ci/base.yml.
# KAS_YAMLS=ci/rb3gen2-core-kit.yml:ci/qcom-distro.yml

# Extra kas-container options for ci/kas-container-shell-helper.sh (string).
# Unset: none.
# KAS_OPTS=--runtime-args --env=MACHINE=qcs9100-ride-sx

# Machine that ci/oe-selftest.sh runs the layer's tests for (machine name).
# Unset: rb3gen2-core-kit.
# MACHINE=qcs9100-ride-sx

# Any non-empty value makes ci/oe-selftest.sh keep git clones job-local under
# TMPDIR (string). Unset: clones persist in DL_DIR/git2.
# GIT_CLONEDIR_JOB_LOCAL=1
